// HLZ-005 — '../x' from inside a subdirectory. The sibling spelling './../x'
// is rejected on purpose: the AST records only parent_levels, so the two are
// indistinguishable after parsing and the formatter could not reprint the
// file faithfully. What was wrong was the diagnostic, not the rejection —
// see errors/parser/parent_path_alias.zy for the message it gives now.
<# ../hlz/salida => s

a = s::nuevo(2)
c = 0
s::poner(a, 1, 5, c)
>> "ruta ../ resuelta: " a "  c=" c ¶
